Subject: [PATCH 6] bpf: isolate and bound each invocation's BPF stack frame

Base: patches 0001-0004 on the pinned Leaf RFC.

Reserve and zero the 16-byte-aligned BPF frame on the invoking kernel stack,
above the private Executive gateway context. Concurrent and nested invocations therefore
have separate live storage; no per-program or per-CPU stack is shared. Release
the reservation in the Executive epilogue. Unprotected Leaf programs retain
their legacy stack allocation.

Derive R10 from the invocation's exactly bounded CSP. Set exact
frame bounds and retain only global/load/store permissions. Track stack
copies, constant offsets and FP-relative access contracts; preserve the key
contract through ARRAY lookup inlining. The gateway already saves full
capability registers. Emit stack accesses through frame-derived capabilities.

Scope remains one ordinary mmapable ARRAY and SOCKET_FILTER, with no pointer
spills, remaining helpers, subprograms or variable pointer arithmetic. This
is not the next milestone's complete-mediation claim: unmarked instructions
still take the existing JIT path, and Leaf's broad RDDC is unchanged.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/net/bpf_jit.h b/arch/arm64/net/bpf_jit.h
index 009b23a48..9142fe65c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/net/bpf_jit.h
+++ b/arch/arm64/net/bpf_jit.h
@@ -19,12 +19,13 @@
 /* Morello A64 capability operands; memory forms use a capability base. */
 #define M64_MOV(Cd, Cn) (0xc2c1d000 | ((Cn) << 5) | (Cd))
 #define M64_ADD(Cd, Cn, Xm) (0xc2a06000 | ((Xm) << 16) | ((Cn) << 5) | (Cd))
+#define M64_SUB_I(Cd, Cn, imm12) (0x02800000 | ((imm12) << 10) | ((Cn) << 5) | (Cd))
 #define M64_BLR(Cn) (0xc2c23000 | ((Cn) << 5))
 #define M64_GCBASE(Xd, Cn) (0xc2c01000 | ((Cn) << 5) | (Xd))
 #define M64_GCVALUE(Xd, Cn) (0xc2c05000 | ((Cn) << 5) | (Xd))
 #define M64_SCVALUE(Cd, Cn, Xm) (0xc2c04000 | ((Xm) << 16) | ((Cn) << 5) | (Cd))
 #define M64_SCBNDSE(Cd, Cn, Xm) (0xc2c02000 | ((Xm) << 16) | ((Cn) << 5) | (Cd))
 #define M64_CLRPERM(Cd, Cn, Xm) (0xc2c0a000 | ((Xm) << 16) | ((Cn) << 5) | (Cd))
 #define M64_MEM(load, size, Rt, Cn) \
 	(0xe2000000 | ((size) << 22) | ((load) << 10) | ((Cn) << 5) | (Rt))
 
